+# Add t and use it to check PlaceBlock's arguments
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker to `pesde.toml`, from Wally
+  through pesde like every other package here:
+  `t = { wally = "osyrisrblx/t", version = "=3.1.1" }` (3.1.1 is the latest version on the Wally
+  index). It installs to `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`, so later remote handlers can use it too.
+- `BlockPlacement.server.luau` now checks PlaceBlock's arguments with one t checker:
+  `t.tuple(t.string, t.intersection(t.Vector3, isNotNaN))`.
+- Adds t to the package table in `README.md`.
+
+## Checks kept
+
+Each check the handler did before still runs, in the same order:
+
+| Before | Now |
+|---|---|
+| `typeof(blockTypeName) ~= "string"` | `t.string` |
+| `typeof(position) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` |
+| `position ~= position` (NaN) | `isNotNaN`, combined with `t.Vector3` through `t.intersection` |
+| Block type exists in `BlockTypes.ByName` | Unchanged |
+| Rate limit (`MIN_INTERVAL`), character and `HumanoidRootPart`, `cell.Y < 0`, cell occupied, `MAX_REACH` | Unchanged |
+
+t checks at runtime only and doesn't narrow Luau types, so the arguments stay `unknown` to the
+type checker. The handler casts them (`:: string`, `:: Vector3`) where they're used, after the
+t check has passed.
+
+## Before testing
+
+1. **Install packages.** With `rojo serve` stopped, run `pesde install` at the repo root. This
+   PR doesn't include the `pesde.lock` update because no install was run while writing it. Commit
+   the updated `pesde.lock` to this branch.
+2. Regenerate the sourcemap so luau-lsp can see the new package:
+   `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`.
+3. Restart `rojo serve` and reconnect the Rojo plugin. Check that `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`
+   is in the place. Without it, `BlockPlacement` errors on require and PlaceBlock never gets
+   created.
+
+## Testing
+
+- [x] `stylua --check src` and `selene src` pass.
+- [ ] `luau-lsp analyze` (the command in the README). Not run yet, because t has to be installed
+  before the require resolves.
+- [ ] Playtest: placing each block type works, and placing out of reach, below Y = 0, on an
+  occupied cell, or faster than every 0.1 s does nothing.
+- [ ] From the client command bar, check that the server places nothing and logs no error for
+  bad arguments:
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer(1, Vector3.zero)`
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("Brick", "x")`
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("Brick", Vector3.new(0/0, 0, 0))`
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("Nope", Vector3.zero)`
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
